sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 67.7/100, audit 2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json; output: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png; organism: Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d6f3c94; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 799d93639f28fa0f81279848de4b8d23b26644a1c8856fdc44c0028d4fc6ba5e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), give Klüver's four form constants; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map | Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number | Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control; reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex with unrestricted branch selection (rhombic angle = argmin gamma_3) and per-panel SELECTED / STABLE-coexisting / IMPOSED-unstable badges, the exact two-regime retino-cortical map with analytic inverse in a full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention (bilateral-mirror mode kept and compared, seam contrast and mirror symmetry quantified), an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and in the visual field via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, rendered wavenumber |k| = q*/d_hyp quantised to integer torus cycles, exact parity with all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs of the upstream fixture with all 133 of its paper-expectation checks counted (121 pass), a comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors, parameter sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition and lateral spread (CLI --sweep), a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry, and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture with its calibration status printed; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values (foveal magnification 10.98 vs the paper's 11.5 mm/deg) and the rendered cortical wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm — both are computed and printed, not corrected | Of the five gallery panels only the rhombic lattice is SELECTED by the cubic amplitude equations; the honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting and tunnel/spiral/cobweb are IMPOSED-unstable, because the bare orientation-overlap cubic coefficients make 2 gamma_3(theta*) < gamma_0 for every parameter value swept (rolls and squares never stable) | The full-field pullback carries a discontinuity on the left horizontal meridian (seam contrast 7-10x for oblique modes) because the theta in (-pi, pi] branch cut maps to a line in cortex; the bilateral-mirror alternative removes the seam but destroys spiral chirality (mirror symmetry 1.000); does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), the full cubic coefficients with firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic feedback (Eq. 5.15), a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), derivation of contoured vs non-contoured from the critical local harmonic (contour_mode is a preset flag), or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations]; other sources: Mescal and Mechanisms of Hallucinations <https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/M/bo3645325.html>, bressloff-v1-form-constants: reference implementation and calibration reports (commit 344863a) <https://github.com/MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.677"^^xsd:double .
}

